  "seiten": {
    "ueber": {
      "pfad": "about",
      "nav": "About the Pictures and Usage",
      "titel": "About the Pictures and How to Use Them",
      "beschreibung": "Where the colouring pages come from and how you may use them: free, public domain (CC0), including for nursery and school.",
      "html": "<h1>About the Pictures and How to Use Them</h1>\n<h2>May I use the pictures?</h2>\n<p>Yes. All colouring pages on this site are <strong>in the public domain</strong> and available under <a href=\"{cc0}\" rel=\"license\">CC0 1.0</a>. You can print them, copy them, hand them out at nursery, at school or in a club, modify them and share them without asking, and without crediting the source. I would still be happy about a link.</p>\n<h2>How were the pictures made?</h2>\n<p>The designs were created with AI support from my own descriptions, then checked by hand, sorted and prepared for printing. Pictures containing text, logos or any resemblance to well-known characters were discarded and made again.</p>\n<p>There are deliberately <strong>no</strong> characters from films, series or books (such as from Disney, Paw Patrol or Pokémon) and no real car brands: these are protected by copyright and trade mark law and must not be freely distributed as colouring pages. Instead you will find original characters and entirely made-up vehicles.</p>\n<h2>What age are they for?</h2>\n<p>Most topics are drawn for children aged 3 and up: thick lines and big areas. Fashion, cars, space and technology are more detailed and intended for children from about 8. The mandalas for adults are very fine and ideal for relaxing.</p>\n<h2>Spotted a mistake or want a new design?</h2>\n<p>If you notice a picture that does not fit, or you would like a particular topic, write to <a href=\"mailto:kontakt@janrenz.de\">kontakt@janrenz.de</a>.</p>"
    },
    "impressum": {
      "pfad": "legal-notice",
      "nav": "Legal Notice",
      "titel": "Legal Notice",
      "beschreibung": "Legal notice for the Malkiste colouring pages website.",
      "html": "<h1>Legal Notice</h1>\n<h2>Information pursuant to § 5 DDG</h2>\n<p>Jan Renz<br>Hans Thoma Str. 3<br>14467 Potsdam<br>Deutschland</p>\n<h2>Contact</h2>\n<p>Email: <a href=\"mailto:kontakt@janrenz.de\">kontakt@janrenz.de</a></p>\n<h2>Responsible for content pursuant to § 18 Abs. 2 MStV</h2>\n<p>Jan Renz<br>Hans Thoma Str. 3<br>14467 Potsdam</p>\n<h2>Liability for links</h2>\n<p>This site contains links to external third-party websites over whose content I have no influence. The respective provider is always responsible for the content of the linked pages. If I become aware of any infringements of the law, the relevant links will be removed immediately.</p>\n<p>This page is a translation. The <a href=\"{impressum_de}\">German version</a> is the legally binding one.</p>"
    },
    "datenschutz": {
      "pfad": "privacy",
      "nav": "Privacy",
      "titel": "Privacy Policy",
      "beschreibung": "Privacy notice: no cookies, anonymous visitor statistics with self-hosted Umami, technically necessary server logs at the host.",
      "html": "<h1>Privacy Notice</h1>\n<h2>In short</h2>\n<p>This site sets <strong>no cookies</strong>, shows no advertising and loads <strong>no content from third parties</strong> (no external fonts). For anonymous visitor statistics I use a self-hosted, cookie-free counting script (see below). There are no forms and no sign-up.</p>\n<h2>Controller</h2>\n<p>Jan Renz, Hans Thoma Str. 3, 14467 Potsdam, Germany, <a href=\"mailto:kontakt@janrenz.de\">kontakt@janrenz.de</a></p>\n<h2>Hosting</h2>\n<p>This site is hosted on GitHub Pages: GitHub Inc., 88 Colin P Kelly Jr St, San Francisco, CA 94107, USA. When you visit the site, the host processes data transmitted by your browser in so-called log files: IP address, date and time of the request, requested address, referrer, HTTP status code, amount of data transferred, and information about your browser and operating system.</p>\n<p>This is necessary to deliver the site and to ensure its stability and security. The legal basis is legitimate interests under Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR. I have no access to these log data myself and do not combine them with other data.</p>\n<p>GitHub is certified under the EU-US Data Privacy Framework and additionally uses EU Standard Contractual Clauses. Further information: <a href=\"https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement\">GitHub General Privacy Statement</a>.</p>\n<h2>Visitor statistics with Umami</h2>\n<p>To find out which colouring pages are popular, I count page views and clicks on “Download PDF”, “Print” and “PNG” using the open-source software Umami. Umami runs on my own server (umami-wwuskowincn5xs0nx5pucyc0.uds.university), sets <strong>no cookies</strong>, stores nothing on your device and does not build profiles across websites.</p>\n<p>The following is recorded: the page visited, the referring page, browser, operating system, device type, screen size, language, and the country, region and city derived from the IP address. The IP address itself is not stored; returning visits are only recognised through a monthly rotating, irreversible hash. If your browser sends a “Do Not Track” signal, nothing is recorded.</p>\n<p>The legal basis is my legitimate interest in privacy-friendly audience measurement (Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR). The statistics server is connected via Cloudflare (Cloudflare Inc., 101 Townsend St, San Francisco, CA 94107, USA), which processes the connection data as a processor and is certified under the EU-US Data Privacy Framework.</p>\n<h2>Contact by email</h2>\n<p>If you send me an email, I process your details only to answer your enquiry (Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR) and delete them as soon as they are no longer needed for that purpose.</p>\n<h2>Your rights</h2>\n<p>You have the right of access, rectification, erasure, restriction of processing, data portability and objection (Arts. 15–21 GDPR), as well as the right to lodge a complaint with a data protection supervisory authority, for example the State Commissioner for Data Protection of Brandenburg (Landesbeauftragte für den Datenschutz Brandenburg).</p>"
    }
  },
